---
// Reader: a programme or service owner choosing where AI could help their team.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { describeServiceHref } from '../../data/contact';
import { teamRecordFull } from '../../data/team';
const context = 'AI-assisted public services';
---
<Base title="AI for public services | Registry Stack" description="Use AI to design a service, adapt it to your rules and let people prepare a request with an assistant you approve. Your institution reviews and approves." ogImagePath="/og-ai.png" ogImageAlt="Registry Stack: Design, adapt and access public services with AI.">
  <SiteHeader current="ai" />
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="hero hero-cover" aria-labelledby="ai-title"><div class="hero-inner"><div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">AI for public services</p>
      <h1 id="ai-title">Design, adapt and access public services with AI.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">AI can help you define a service and prepare changes to implement it. It can also help people make a request. You approve the rules and the changes to your service.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href={describeServiceHref(context)} data-journey="service-inquiry">Discuss your service</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="#uses">See the three ways AI can help</a></div>
    </div></div></section>

    <section class="section" id="uses" aria-labelledby="uses-title"><div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="uses-title">Choose the use of AI that matches your need.</h2></div>
      <div class="ai-paths">
        <article><p class="eyebrow">Service design</p><h3>Prepare a brief and test a prototype</h3><p>Use research and your service’s requirements to work through the service with staff and applicants. The result is a reviewed brief that goes to your delivery team. AI helps with the research and the drafting. People review the brief.</p><p class="path-status">We offer this as a scoped engagement, mainly through our partners.</p><a class="inline-cta" href="/ai/service-design/">Read about AI-assisted service design <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
        <article><p class="eyebrow">Implementation</p><h3>Adapt a service to your rules</h3><p>We use AI to draft configuration, test cases and guidance. We check each draft. Your team approves the changes before release.</p><p class="path-status">Aubex offers this as part of Pilot register implementation, a paid service.</p><a class="inline-cta" href="/customization/">Read how we use AI in implementation <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
        <article id="citizen-access"><p class="eyebrow">Citizen access</p><h3>Help people prepare a request</h3><p>An assistant that you approve reads only the details you allow. It prepares a draft. The person checks the draft and submits it on your official website.</p><p>The assistant cannot submit a request, approve it or change a record. <a href="/products/base-registry/">Base Registry Engine</a> is the software that keeps your register’s records.</p><p class="path-status">This works with a configured Base Registry Engine service.</p><a class="inline-cta" href="/ai/citizen-access/">See the citizen access example <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="control-title"><div class="section-inner approach-split">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="control-title">Your staff set the rules.</h2><p>AI can propose a design or draft a change. You confirm the service rules. You review and approve implementation changes.</p><p>Your configured registry service runs without an AI model. For citizen access, you choose which assistants may connect. You also choose what they can read and prepare.</p><a class="inline-cta" href="/architecture/headless/">See how this fits your existing systems <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
      <div class="editorial-callout"><p class="eyebrow">Authoring tool · Preview</p><h3>Registry Studio</h3><p>Registry Studio is a workspace where you and your technical team review records, service steps and proposed changes. It can use your existing documents to prepare a draft brief for review.</p><a class="inline-cta" href="/products/studio/">Read about Registry Studio <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="team-title"><div class="section-inner approach-split">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="team-title">Aubex’s founder has long experience with government registries.</h2><p>{teamRecordFull}</p><p>Registry Stack’s core runtime software is open source under the Apache-2.0 licence. Your own team or another provider you choose can inspect it, adapt it and run it. Or we can host and operate the service for you. We quote hosting and operation separately in a proposal. We also offer paid implementation and paid support.</p></div>
      <div class="editorial-callout"><h3>Inspect the software and its boundaries</h3><ul class="check-links"><li><a href="https://github.com/registrystack/registry-stack">Source code and releases on GitHub</a></li><li><a href="https://docs.registrystack.org/security/#an-ai-assistant-acting-for-a-citizen">Security model for an AI assistant acting for a citizen</a></li><li><a href="/pricing/">Implementation and pricing</a></li></ul></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="final-cta" aria-labelledby="next-title"><div class="section-inner"><h2 id="next-title">Start with one service.</h2><p>Describe a service you plan, or bring a form or process you want to adapt. We then agree three things with you: what to evaluate, who reviews it and what your team receives.</p><div class="section-links"><a class="button button-primary" href={describeServiceHref(context)} data-journey="service-inquiry">Discuss your service</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/pricing/">See implementation and pricing</a></div></div></section>
  </main><SiteFooter />
</Base>
<style>
  .ai-paths { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: clamp(24px, 4vw, 48px); }
  .ai-paths article { border-top: 2px solid var(--registry-blue); display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: start; padding-top: 24px; }
  .ai-paths h3 { font-size: var(--type-xl); }
  .ai-paths .path-status { font-size: var(--type-sm); }
  .ai-paths .inline-cta { margin-top: auto; }
  .check-links { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .check-links li { border-top: 1px solid var(--registry-rule); padding: 14px 0; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { .ai-paths { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
